# .rules — Nimbus eCommerce Platform

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PROJECT RULES & CONVENTIONS
# Nimbus eCommerce Platform
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── TECH STACK ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
frontend: Next.js 13 (App Router) + React 18 + TypeScript
styling: Tailwind CSS + Shadcn UI + tailwindcss-animate
icons: lucide-react
database: Supabase (PostgreSQL) + @supabase/supabase-js
auth: Supabase Auth (email/password, JWT)
charts: recharts
forms: react-hook-form + zod
toasts: sonner

# ─── FORBIDDEN ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
no_purple: NEVER use purple, indigo, or violet hues unless explicitly requested
no_external_ui_libs: Do NOT install UI theme/icon libraries beyond Shadcn + lucide-react
no_supabase_cli: NEVER use the Supabase CLI — use MCP tools only
no_raw_ddl: NEVER run DDL outside mcp__supabase__apply_migration
no_drop: NEVER DROP tables or DELETE columns — data loss is unacceptable
no_transactions: NEVER use BEGIN/COMMIT/ROLLBACK (DO $$ blocks are OK)
no_env_exports: NEVER reference or expose .env values in responses
no_emojis: NEVER use emojis in responses or code comments

# ─── DATABASE RULES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
rls_required: EVERY table must have RLS enabled
policy_pattern: 4 separate policies (SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE) — never FOR ALL
owner_default: user_id columns must DEFAULT auth.uid()
anon_access: no-auth apps use TO anon, authenticated; auth apps use TO authenticated
maybeSingle: use maybeSingle() for zero-or-one queries, never single()
idempotent: migrations must be safe to re-run (IF NOT EXISTS, DROP POLICY IF EXISTS)

# ─── CODE CONVENTIONS ───────────────────────────────────────────
server_first: Default to Server Components; add "use client" only when needed
strict_ts: TypeScript strict mode — explicit types on all function params
import_all: Every referenced symbol must have a matching import
no_comments: Default to no comments — only explain non-obvious WHY
no_dead_code: Delete replaced code; no orphaned files or commented-out blocks
match_codebase: Match existing naming, layout, and error-handling patterns
reuse_first: Search for existing utilities before writing new ones
file_size: Keep files at a manageable size for readability

# ─── DESIGN RULES ──────────────────────────────────────────────
color_system: 6+ color ramps (primary, secondary, accent, success, warning, error)
spacing: 8px spacing system
line_height: 150% body, 120% headings
font_weights: 3 weights maximum
responsive: Mobile-first, breakpoints at sm/md/lg/xl
contrast: WCAG AA contrast ratios on all backgrounds
animations: Tasteful micro-interactions, hover states, transitions
no_cookie_cutter: Designs must be beautiful and production-worthy

# ─── BUILD & VERIFY ─────────────────────────────────────────────
build_required: Run "npm run build" before completing any task
fix_failures: Fix build/typecheck errors before reporting done
no_false_success: Never claim success when checks show failures
verify_ui: Use the dev server to verify UI changes in browser
report_honestly: Describe problems in plain words — never hide failures

# ─── AUTH RULES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
email_password_only: Default to Supabase email/password — no magic links or social
email_confirmation_off: Email confirmation stays OFF
build_full_flow: If auth is needed, build both sign-in AND sign-up
onauth_deadlock: Wrap async work in onAuthStateChange in IIFE

# ─── EDGE FUNCTIONS ─────────────────────────────────────────────
cors_required: Every response must include the full CORS header set
try_catch: Always wrap function body in try/catch
npm_prefix: Use npm: or jsr: prefixes — never bare specifiers
no_deno_std: Use Deno.serve, never import from deno.land/std
write_first: Write function to disk BEFORE deploying via MCP tool

# ─── SECURITY ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
jwt_auth: JWT-based authentication
role_permissions: Role-based access via customers.role column
audit_logs: All admin actions should be traceable
xss_protection: React escapes by default; never dangerouslySetInnerHTML
sql_injection: Supabase client uses parameterized queries
rate_limiting: Apply at edge function level for sensitive endpoints

# ─── USER ROLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# customer         — shop, cart, checkout, own orders/wishlist/addresses
# admin            — full access + admin dashboard
# sales_manager    — orders, CRM, reports (read)
# warehouse_manager — inventory, shipping, stock adjustments
# accountant       — invoices, financial reports

# ─── TEST ACCOUNTS ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# customer@nimbus.shop    / NimbusTest2025!
# admin@nimbus.shop       / NimbusTest2025!
# sales@nimbus.shop       / NimbusTest2025!
# warehouse@nimbus.shop   / NimbusTest2025!
# accountant@nimbus.shop  / NimbusTest2025!
